# Review tiers of the fork (tier numbers: the repository layout specification, section 7).
# The last matching line wins. This file only takes effect once the repository setting
# "require review from Code Owners" is on; that setting is changed separately by the lead.
#
# Tier 2: every path needs one approval from a code owner other than the author.
# Teammate accounts are added to this line when the settings are applied.
*                     @pengchenglu1997
#
# Tier 3: the lead alone.
/AGENTS.md            @pengchenglu1997
/rl/METHOD.md         @pengchenglu1997
/rl/best.tsv          @pengchenglu1997
/.github/workflows/   @pengchenglu1997
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @pengchenglu1997
# The root .gitattributes (a TEAM path) is tier 3: it changes how every file is stored and compared, so only the lead
# approves it. F1 treats it like any other team path.
/.gitattributes       @pengchenglu1997
# All of rl/tools/ is tier 3. F1 runs check_pr.py and common.py of the base commit, and the other files of the folder (the
# fixtures, scrub_allow.txt, the other checks) decide what the rest of the checks accept. Without this line one teammate
# approval could change a rule that judges the same pull request.
/rl/tools/            @pengchenglu1997
# The Claude Code project settings and hook (.claude/, a TEAM path) are tier 3: they decide which commands ask the human.
/.claude/             @pengchenglu1997
#
# Tier 1 (regenerated README blocks only) is not a path rule and has no line here.
